{"id":"s4.4.3","slug":"sum-reciprocals-triangular-numbers","title":"Sum of the Reciprocals of Triangular Numbers","content":"<p class=\"mb-4\">This problem involves finding the sum of the reciprocals of a series of consecutive triangular numbers. The solution relies on knowing the starting term number ($n$) and the ending term number ($m$) of the triangular numbers in the sequence.</p><p class=\"text-center font-bold mb-4\">$\\frac{1}{T_n} + \\frac{1}{T_{n+1}} + \\dots + \\frac{1}{T_m} = 2(\\frac{1}{n} - \\frac{1}{m+1})$</p><p>For example, $\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{21}$ corresponds to the sum from the 3rd to the 6th triangular number. So, $n=3$ and $m=6$. The sum is $2(\\frac{1}{3} - \\frac{1}{7}) = \\frac{8}{21}$.</p>","summary":"This problem involves finding the sum of the reciprocals of a series of consecutive triangular numbers.","generation_guideline":"Generate a sum of a series of reciprocals of triangular numbers.","questions":[{"id":1,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15}$.","answer":"4/5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":2,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10}$.","answer":"3/5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":3,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{21}$.","answer":"5/7","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":4,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{21}$.","answer":"8/21","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":5,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15}$.","answer":"1/3","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":6,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{1} + \\frac{1}{3} + \\frac{1}{6} + \\frac{1}{10}$.","answer":"8/5","kind":"exact","tags":["fractions","sequences"]},{"id":7,"text":"Calculate $\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{21} + \\frac{1}{28}$.","answer":"1/4","k